      "heading": "What Quickler does and does not do",
      "html": "<p>Quickler suits the physical walk. It keeps your readings, photos and Faults, with a time on each. That is useful proof for insurers, landlords and internal audit.</p><p>It does not test the network, read switch settings or check logical security. If your check is a network audit, it is not the tool for that half.</p><p><strong>Honest note:</strong> the check is only as good as the person doing it. Quickler makes the proof easy to gather. It does not decide if the room passes. <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">Ask us</a> to see it work.</p>"
