      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What should a comms room checklist include?</h3><p>Power: UPS status, load, battery age, last self-test. Temperature: room reading, aircon running, clean filters. Cabling: tidy and labelled, airflow clear. Housekeeping: clear floor, nothing combustible, no water. Access: door locks and the access list is current. Record each with a reading or photo.</p><h3>How often should a server room be inspected?</h3><p>Often monthly or quarterly. It depends on how important the room is, and what your insurer or ISO 27001 controls ask for. Check temperature more often, or monitor it all the time.</p><h3>Can I do a server room check in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Each item arrives in your usual chat. Reply with a reading, voice note or photo. Quickler writes the record. No app. No login. It records the physical check, not a network audit.</p><h3>Does it count towards ISO 27001?</h3><p>It gives proof for several ISO 27001:2022 Annex A physical controls, such as secure areas and equipment protection. It is one input to an audit. A qualified auditor decides certification.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/data-centre-audit-software-uk.html\">Data centre audit software</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/iso-27001-physical-security-audit-uk.html\">ISO 27001 physical security audit</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/dr-site-audit-checklist-uk.html\">DR site audit checklist</a></li></ul>"
